<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Sons of Gwalia net loss A$128.39 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Sons of Gwalia net loss A$128.39 mln.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		     70.92 vs 49.79</p>
<p>    Net			     loss  128.39 vs profit 30.41</p>
<p>    Abnormal (after-tax)	loss  167.78 vs nil</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			 nil vs 12.5</p>
<p>NOTE: Gold miner Sons of Gwalia Ltd said it planned at 12.5 cents per share return of capital in lieu of paying a final dividend. The company said the abnormal losses reflected a write-down of mining and explorations property.  </p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	     12.5 vs 25.0</p>
<p>    Sales				  333.83 vs 201.90</p>
<p>    Other income			  30.07 vs 7.31</p>
<p>    Shr (A$)		  loss	1.255 vs 0.397</p>
<p>    Tax				     28.39 vs 19.05</p>
<p>    Interest				12.38 vs 3.83</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  40.39 vs 26.00</p>
<p>    Minorities			     3.13 vs 0.32</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
